      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "Benday.EfCore.Adapters.CoreFieldsAdapterBase<TModel, TEntity, TIdentity>",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Benday.EfCore.Adapters.CoreFieldsAdapterBase-3.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Adapter base for CoreFields models/entities. Copies the framework-managed\nfields — Status, the four audit fields, and the optimistic-concurrency\ntoken (plus identity, entity → model) — automatically in both directions,\nleaving subclasses to override only <code>PerformAdapt</code> for their own\nproperties. This is the adapter-tier parallel to\n<xref href=\"Benday.EfCore.Entities.CoreFieldsEntityBase%601\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>,\n<xref href=\"Benday.EfCore.DomainModels.CoreFieldsDomainModelBase%601\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>, and the\nCoreFields service-layer base.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/Benday.EfCore.Adapters.CoreFieldsAdapterBase-3.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"10\">The framework copy runs via the <xref href=\"Benday.EfCore.Adapters.AdapterBase%603.CopyFrameworkFields(%600%2c%601)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>\nhook, so the override surface is identical to a plain adapter: you still\nonly implement <code>PerformAdapt</code>.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/Benday.EfCore.Adapters.CoreFieldsAdapterBase-3.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"14\">Escape hatches: override <code>CopyFrameworkFields</code> to take full control,\nand call the granular <xref href=\"Benday.EfCore.Adapters.CoreFieldsAdapterBase%603.CopyAuditFields(%600%2c%601)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>,\n<xref href=\"Benday.EfCore.Adapters.CoreFieldsAdapterBase%603.CopyStatus(%600%2c%601)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>, and\n<xref href=\"Benday.EfCore.Adapters.CoreFieldsAdapterBase%603.CopyConcurrencyToken(%600%2c%601)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> helpers to reuse only\nthe pieces you want. Override everything and you're on your own — nothing\nforces the helpers on you.</p>\n"
    },
