      "Title": "Benday.EfCore.Migrations.DefaultDesignTimeDbContextFactory<TContext>",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Benday.EfCore.Migrations.DefaultDesignTimeDbContextFactory-1.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Provider-agnostic design-time DbContext factory base so the EF Core CLI\n(<code>dotnet ef</code>) can construct a context for generating migrations. Reads a\nnamed connection string (default: &quot;default&quot;) from appsettings.json plus\nenvironment-specific overrides and environment variables.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/Benday.EfCore.Migrations.DefaultDesignTimeDbContextFactory-1.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"6\">Provider packages supply the actual provider wiring by overriding\n<xref href=\"Benday.EfCore.Migrations.DefaultDesignTimeDbContextFactory%601.ConfigureProvider(Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.DbContextOptionsBuilder%7b%600%7d%2cSystem.String)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> (for example,\n<code>SqlServerDesignTimeDbContextFactory</code> in Benday.EfCore.SqlServer calls\n<code>UseSqlServer</code>). Concrete factories override\n<xref href=\"Benday.EfCore.Migrations.DefaultDesignTimeDbContextFactory%601.Create(Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.DbContextOptions%7b%600%7d)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> to construct the context.</p>\n"
